--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 0220 asked upstream for `ZOTEUS_EMBEDDING_DTYPE`, a global precision
knob. That ask is withdrawn. Its motivating premise was false and its shape was
wrong, and both were established by measurement rather than by argument — see
0220's log and `verification/DEVICE-AUTO-0220.md`.

What survives 0220 is the observation, not the remedy: the shipped local path
runs at full precision because nobody passes an options object, not because
anyone chose fp32. Measured on the default model, `all-MiniLM-L6-v2`, warm: the
resident cost of the load falls 143,7 MB to 69,1 MB at q8, and load time 415,2 ms
to 191,1 ms. The problem is real. A standalone env var is not the answer to it.

**Why not a knob.** Precision cannot travel alone. `dtype` resolves through
`DEFAULT_DTYPE_SUFFIX_MAPPING` to a filename, so it is a bet on one repo's naming
that some repos lose outright (`intfloat/multilingual-e5-small` publishes nothing
the knob can address but fp32, verified in 0261). Pooling is per-model and four
of six sweep candidates want `cls` where the drivers hardcode `mean` (0421).
Input templates are per-model, and e5 without its prefixes measures worse than an
English model that never needed any. A user handed a precision knob and none of
the rest gets a setting whose most likely outcome is a wrong conclusion about a
good model.

Zotero core reached the same place independently: `dtype`, `pooling`,
`queryPrefix`, `passagePrefix` and `maxTokens` are fields of a curated model
entry, the preference names the entry, and there is no user-facing precision knob
anywhere (`zotero/zotero#6012`).

So the upstream ask is the entry, and the knob is its id.

## Relevant files

- `tickets/0220-...erg` — the withdrawn ask, its four premise corrections, and the
  measurements that survive
- `verification/DEVICE-AUTO-0220.md` — the device finding, which travels
  separately and is not part of this ask
- `bench/models.json` + `bench/registry.mjs` / `registry.py` — this repo's own
  registry, the shape being proposed
- `GOVERNANCE.md` — form: design-sized work goes as an issue he builds, five for
  five

## Actions

1. Wait for the measurements. This ask is only worth making with a table behind
   it, which is what 0262/0263 produce. Filing it earlier spends his attention on
   a design argument with no evidence under it.
2. Draft it as an ISSUE, not a pull request. It decides which models the project
   supports and what its configuration surface looks like — design-sized by
   GOVERNANCE.md's test, and the asymmetry there reads five for five.
3. Lead with the defect, not the design: the local path is pinned to one model
   that Zotero core files under "Models for testing", so a non-English library
   cannot be served at all. Precision is a consequence of the registry, never its
   headline.
4. Carry the per-model evidence: for each candidate, dtype availability probed
   against the repo, pooling read off its own `1_Pooling/config.json`, input
   template, max sequence, licence, and the measured cost and recall.
5. Point at a prototype rather than offering one, per the issue #33 precedent.
6. Say what the registry must NOT be: an untyped options bag. Every field in one
   degrades retrieval silently when wrong, which reads as the model being worse
   rather than as a bug.
7. Frame what ships to the user as a curated menu, Zotero core's shape: each
   entry pins model, dtype, pooling, input template and normalize; the user
   picks by what the facets mean to them — languages, RAM cost, speed,
   retrieval quality, hardware requirement — never by mechanics. An entry
   whose only loadable rung needs a GPU is labelled so; a larger model
   rejected for the default (the registry's size rejections) can stand in the
   menu as a non-default entry for capable hardware, if the evidence supports
   one.

## Test

- The claim that a non-English library is unserved is checked before it is sent:
  the local model is hardcoded, `ZOTEUS_EMBEDDING_MODEL` reaches only the API
  providers, and the comment at that call site says so.
- Every per-model value in the issue traces to a probe or a model card, none
  inferred. This is the discipline 0421 established after four of six candidates
  came out `cls` against an assumption of `mean`.

## Invariants

- No precision knob is proposed, in the issue or in any prototype it points at.
- Nothing about this repository's internal governance enters the issue text
  (GOVERNANCE.md's disclosure rule). The repository is public and he reads it.
- The device finding is not folded in, and it is not filed anywhere either.
  Nobody passes `device: 'auto'`, so it is not a defect in the maintainer's code;
  where it is a defect it is already huggingface/transformers.js#1642.

## Exit criteria

- [x] 0262/0263 have produced the candidate table this ask rests on
- [ ] Issue drafted, read as sent, and shown to the author before anything is
      filed
- [ ] Filed upstream, or explicitly deferred with the reason recorded here
